# CO-WP-DEVELOPMENT-MODE-003 — Module-Complete Development

Status: **EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY** · Product Owner authority · Governing  
**Supersedes:** CO-WP-DEVELOPMENT-MODE-002 (retired as governing cadence)  
Companion: CO-WP-103B UX Constitution · CO-WP-CONSTITUTION-001 · `enterprise-wealth-partner-app.mdc`

## Development strategy

**Develop complete modules.**  
**Do NOT develop isolated screens.**

The Wealth Partner App is an **Enterprise Companion** over Catalyst One.

**Catalyst One thinks. The Wealth Partner App presents.**

## Modules (complete one before the next)

1. **Home**
2. **Business**
3. **Saarthi**
4. **Private**
5. **More**

Map to primary companion shell destinations. Do not invent alternate primary modules without Product Owner approval.

## Module completion (Definition of Done)

A module is **complete** only when it includes **all** of:

| Required |
|----------|
| All related screens |
| Navigation |
| Empty states |
| Loading states |
| Skeleton loaders |
| Interactions |
| Animations |
| Page transitions |
| Responsive layouts |
| Enterprise DTO integration |
| Design consistency |
| Dark theme compliance |
| Accessibility |
| Error states |
| Enterprise Unavailable handling |

**Do not stop after every screen.**  
**Stop only after the complete module has been implemented.**

## Enterprise Experience Engine

**Home must NOT own content.** Home renders Enterprise Experience DTOs.

Examples: Hero Carousel · Recommended Actions · Today’s Highlights · Business Feed · Notifications · Personalisation · Digital Visiting Card.

Everything must be configurable from Catalyst One.

## Product Workspace

Every financial product opens into an **Enterprise Product Workspace**.

Examples: Home Loan · LAP · Business Loan · Mutual Fund · Insurance · Fixed Deposit · future products.

**The Wealth Partner App must never hardcode product pages.**

Catalyst One owns: Banner · Description · Rates · Documents · Lenders · Training · Marketing · Calculators · CTA.

The app renders.

## Zero Trust

Every screen must consume **Partner-scoped Enterprise APIs**.

- No employee APIs  
- No local business logic  
- No duplicated calculations  

## Design philosophy

Every module must follow the approved UX Constitution:

Premium · Elegant · Dark Theme · Consumer FinTech quality.

Every morning the app should feel enjoyable to open.

## Certification cadence

```text
Complete Module
  → Product Owner Review
  → Product Owner Refinements
  → Certification
  → Freeze
  → Deployment (PO-approved only)
  → Next Module
```

## Deployment

- Do **NOT** deploy after every screen.  
- Do **NOT** deploy after every sprint.  
- Deploy **only** after the complete module has been reviewed and **approved** by the Product Owner.

## Current status

| Module | Status |
|--------|--------|
| **Home** | Implementation Complete · WAVE-001 confirm · Awaiting Product Owner Module Certification |
| **Business** | **In progress** under **CO-WP-DEVELOPMENT-WAVE-001** (PO authorised) |
| Saarthi · Private · More | WAVE-001 queue after Business |

**EEE:** Still **DO NOT IMPLEMENT** (CO-WP-ARCHITECTURE-UPDATE-001). WAVE-001 builds companion modules only — not Experience Center.

**Deploy:** Not until Product Owner reviews completed modules (WAVE-001).

## Non-negotiable

The Wealth Partner App is **NOT** another CRM.  
It is **NOT** another Operating System.  
It is the **Enterprise Companion** to Catalyst One.

If Catalyst One is unavailable, the Wealth Partner App should have almost nothing meaningful to do except authenticate the user and communicate that **Enterprise Services are unavailable**.

## Agent behaviour

1. Prefer completing the **current module** over shipping isolated screens.  
2. Follow **CO-WP-DEVELOPMENT-WAVE-001** priority (Home → Business → Saarthi → Private → More). Business module builds are authorised; do not wait for EEE.  
3. Never hardcode product pages or Experience content as companion SSOT.  
4. Never call employee APIs or duplicate Enterprise calculations.  
5. Do not deploy without Product Owner approval.  
6. Do **not** implement Enterprise Experience Engine / Experience Center in WAVE-001. Use placeholder DTOs where Partner Business APIs are incomplete.

